>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `BEST_TAC`

``` hol4
classicalLib.BEST_TAC : thm list -> tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Solves a goal by best-first classical search.

`BEST_TAC thms` safely saturates the whole state, then expands the first
open goal with the fast instantiating or unsafe cascade. Its frontier
orders states by the total normalized syntactic size of their
open goals. It eagerly enumerates children and does not use the dynamic
per-goal pruning of depth-first search. Expanded states are limited by
`clasetSearch.node_limit`, whose default is 100000; a non-positive value
disables that limit.

The theorem list locally modifies the current classical rule set. The
markers `SIntro`, `Intro`, `SElim`, `Elim`, `SDest`, `Dest` and `Del` add
or remove rules. Every unmarked theorem is inserted as an assumption before
search starts. Content-bearing generic simplifier wrappers are unwrapped
and inserted; inert generic controls are ignored.

This tactic succeeds only after all goals have been solved and the proof
has been replayed.

### Failure

Fails when the frontier is exhausted or the node limit is reached without
a complete proof. Malformed extra rules can also fail during marker
processing.

### Example

``` hol4
Theorem best_tac_example:
  (p /\ q ==> r) ==> p ==> q ==> r
Proof
  classicalLib.BEST_TAC []
QED
```

